A routine that returns nonzero has work left, and the caller retries afterwards.

The table below is centred by SkoolKit's own keyword, which is not this project's
prose and is not reported.

#TABLE(default,centre,centre)
{ =h A | =h B }
{ one | two }
TABLE#

Nothing here writes zeros or front-end, because a form the registry qualifies by
grammatical role is a hand pass and this check does not decide it.
